{
  "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1_title",
      "text": "Most hackathon demos are a screen recording and an apology. This tool turns a project into a finished demo video in one command. This is what that command produces.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "card",
        "template": "title"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_problem",
      "text": "The usual demo is recorded at midnight, in one take, with someone whispering over it. If the app stalls, the take is ruined, and fixing one sentence means recording everything again.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "card",
        "template": "title-left",
        "vars": {
          "kicker": "THE USUAL DEMO",
          "name": "RECORDED AT MIDNIGHT.",
          "tagline": "ONE TAKE, WHISPERED OVER, UPLOADED AS-IS.",
          "sub": "A stalled app ruins the take. A rushed sentence hides the screen.",
          "note": "Fixing one line means recording everything again.",
          "meta": "the problem: no script &middot; no retakes &middot; no proof it works"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_term",
      "text": "So instead, you write the story once: a hook, a problem, the product working, proof, and a close. Each part gets its own voiceover, so nothing has to be perfect in one take. Change one sentence later and only that sentence is recorded again.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "term",
        "title": "democut - one command to a finished demo",
        "lines": [
          {
            "at": 0.4,
            "type": "cmd",
            "text": "./scripts/run.sh",
            "cps": 16
          },
          {
            "at": 2.0,
            "text": "[tts]    s1_title    narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 2.9,
            "text": "[tts]    s2_problem  narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 3.8,
            "text": "[tts]    s3_term     narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 4.7,
            "text": "[tts]    s4_app      narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 5.6,
            "text": "[tts]    s5_deep     narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 6.5,
            "text": "[tts]    s6_proof    narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 7.4,
            "text": "[tts]    s7_close    narration",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 8.6,
            "type": "rule"
          },
          {
            "at": 9.6,
            "text": "[rec]    card    s1_title     ok",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 10.5,
            "text": "[rec]    card    s2_problem   ok",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 11.4,
            "text": "[rec]    term    s3_term      scripted lines",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 12.3,
            "text": "[rec]    page    s4_app       7 actions",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 13.2,
            "text": "[rec]    page    s5_deep      6 actions",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 14.1,
            "text": "[rec]    term    s6_proof     scripted lines",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 15.0,
            "text": "[rec]    card    s7_close     ok",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 16.2,
            "text": "[build]  trim -> concat -> subtitles -> loudnorm",
            "cls": "white"
          },
          {
            "at": 17.6,
            "text": "[qa]     contact sheet  -  no issues",
            "cls": "green"
          },
          {
            "at": 19.0,
            "text": "out/demo.mp4   1080p30   ready",
            "cls": "green",
            "flash": "g"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_app",
      "text": "The video shows the real app, not screenshots. It scrolls, it clicks, it types the way a customer would on their first day, and the voiceover stays in step because every scene is timed to the line that describes it.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "page",
        "src": "app/index.html",
        "zoom": 1.5,
        "wait_for": [
          "text=Ship with confidence"
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "action": "move",
            "x": 0.5,
            "y": 0.12,
            "dur": 0.7
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".stats",
            "dur": 1.2,
            "after": 0.6
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".runs",
            "dur": 1.2,
            "cue": 2
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".activity",
            "dur": 1.1,
            "after": 0.5
          }
        ],
        "take": "app"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_deep",
      "text": "You decide where it looks and when. Point it at a section, wait for the page to load, type in the search box, press the button. If something is missing, the run tells you instead of quietly filming an empty screen. What ends up in the video is the actual page, at full size, doing the work.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "page",
        "take": "app",
        "actions": [
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "y": 0.0,
            "dur": 1.0,
            "cue": 2
          },
          {
            "action": "click",
            "sel": "#search",
            "after": 0.3
          },
          {
            "action": "type",
            "sel": "#search",
            "text": "rollback safety",
            "cps": 16
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".runs",
            "dur": 1.1,
            "cue": 3
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".cta",
            "dur": 1.2,
            "cue": 4
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_proof",
      "text": "Before you upload, look at what you made. The tool lays out a sheet of frames, one from every part of the video, so a blank screen or a frozen moment shows up at a glance. It also keeps a frame from the middle of each scene, where a mismatch between the picture and the voice is easiest to catch.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "term",
        "title": "democut - verify the result",
        "lines": [
          {
            "at": 0.4,
            "type": "cmd",
            "text": "./scripts/run.sh --project example",
            "cps": 16
          },
          {
            "at": 3.0,
            "text": "[qa]  file       out/demo.mp4",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 5.0,
            "text": "[qa]  video      1920x1080  30fps  h264",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 7.0,
            "text": "[qa]  audio      aac  48000Hz  loudness checked",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 9.4,
            "text": "[qa]  duration   reported - length follows the product",
            "cls": "white"
          },
          {
            "at": 12.0,
            "type": "rule"
          },
          {
            "at": 13.2,
            "text": "[qa]  contact    qa/contact_sheet.jpg  (16 frames)",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 15.8,
            "text": "[qa]  frames     qa/frames/*.jpg  (one per segment)",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 18.4,
            "text": "[qa]  black gaps  none    short clips  none",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 21.0,
            "text": "PASS  no issues",
            "cls": "green",
            "flash": "g"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_close",
      "text": "One file comes out at the end, with the voiceover and the subtitles already in it, ready to upload. Copy this folder into your project, rewrite the story in your own words, point it at your product, and you have a demo without opening a video editor.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "card",
        "template": "close"
      }
    }
  ]
}
